theo-pod (t-169): clear the quantized spectrum before decoding a frame

huffspec_fxp() decodes the sections into quantSpec[], then rescales every
band of the window. Bands that no section covers (a corrupt section table)
keep the previous frame's values, or whatever the memory shared with
quantSpec[] holds. Their magnitude is not part of the frame's max, so
esc_iquant_scaling() takes the table path for them and indexes
inverseQuantTable[] past its end. The spectrum (1024 Int16) is now zeroed
first; missing coefficients are zero, as ISO/IEC 14496-3 implies. Found by
the host fuzzer (ASan global-buffer-overflow in esc_iquant_scaling);
regression input tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-stale-spectrum.bin.

